(6251829, 923479, 103032, '<td valign="top">I like what you were going for here.  The composition is good with the leading lines of the street and tracks. The motion blur of the passing train on the right is great.  However, the blurriness of the buildings takes away from the motion blur effect.  It looks like you were standing on the sidewalk unbraced.  For maximum effect of the motion blur of the trains and the person on the left, next time you may want to bring along a tripod or at least brace yourself against the wall to keep the stationary objects in focus for this type of shot. Just my humble opinion and critique, FWIW.</td>', 'I like what you were going for here.  The composition is good with the leading lines of the street and tracks. The motion blur of the passing train on the right is great.  However, the blurriness of the buildings takes away from the motion blur effect.  It looks like you were standing on the sidewalk unbraced.  For maximum effect of the motion blur of the trains and the person on the left, next time you may want to bring along a tripod or at least brace yourself against the wall to keep the stationary objects in focus for this type of shot. Just my humble opinion and critique, FWIW.', '2010-12-12 16:20:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(6251835, 924097, 103032, '<td valign="top">This is creative.  A revolving door, right?  Guessing you used some type of suction cup mount for the camera.  This is cool with the "faded" blurred feet.</td>', 'This is creative.  A revolving door, right?  Guessing you used some type of suction cup mount for the camera.  This is cool with the "faded" blurred feet.', '2010-12-12 16:24:22.000000', NULL, 1),
