(6254536, 924046, 41864, '<td valign="top">Congrats on your ribbon, this got a 9 from me. Love it.</td>', 'Congrats on your ribbon, this got a 9 from me. Love it.', '2010-12-15 04:14:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(6254548, 924080, 20799, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on the great finish for a great shot (checked for sensor dust :). Interesting point about the light change. Although these days we have long winter sunsets at these latitudes, I''ve also noticed how the lighting conditions can be tricky and uneven.</td>', 'Congratulations on the great finish for a great shot (checked for sensor dust :). Interesting point about the light change. Although these days we have long winter sunsets at these latitudes, I''ve also noticed how the lighting conditions can be tricky and uneven.', '2010-12-15 04:26:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(6254553, 923997, 124177, '<td valign="top">Thank you for all the comments and for voting. I''m quite satisfied with the result, considering that I started taking pictures with a SLR two weeks ago.<br/> <br/>I had been taking pictures of buildings and other stuff at night, and was on my way home when I came across this statue. I felt straight away that it was a perfect subject, considering the posture and the Christmas light in the back.<br/> <br/>While fixing my camera to a tripod, I set the shutter speed to 4 seconds. It was a bit difficult the get the timing right, but the effect was achieved by zooming in during exposure. It could have been a bit better, but it was also a bit difficult to get the lights in the back to be perfectly aligned.<br/> <br/>I believe I''m in a fast track to learning SLR, but I would really appreciate some tips on how I could have done this better.</td>', 'Thank you for all the comments and for voting. I''m quite satisfied with the result, considering that I started taking pictures with a SLR two weeks ago. I had been taking pictures of buildings and other stuff at night, and was on my way home when I came across this statue. I felt straight away that it was a perfect subject, considering the posture and the Christmas light in the back. While fixing my camera to a tripod, I set the shutter speed to 4 seconds. It was a bit difficult the get the timing right, but the effect was achieved by zooming in during exposure. It could have been a bit better, but it was also a bit difficult to get the lights in the back to be perfectly aligned. I believe I''m in a fast track to learning SLR, but I would really appreciate some tips on how I could have done this better.', '2010-12-15 04:39:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(6254582, 924046, 92847, '<td valign="top">Huge congratulations!! Very well deserved ribbon!</td>', 'Huge congratulations!! Very well deserved ribbon!', '2010-12-15 05:51:18.000000', NULL, 0),
